quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  28,78,He said: ‘I have indeed been given (all) this (wealth) because of the knowledge (and expertise) I possess.’ Did he not know that Allah had already destroyed before him many generations who were far mightier than him in power and greater in accumulating (wealth)? And the guilty will not be questioned about (their excuse for) their sins.
  28,79,"So he emerged before his people in his adornment. Those who desired the life of this world said: ‘We wish we had the likes of what Qarun (Korah) has been given! Indeed, he is a possessor of great fortune.’"
  28,80,But those gifted with knowledge said: ‘Woe to you! Allah’s reward is better for someone who believes and acts righteously. But no one will receive it except the patient.’
  28,81,"So We caused the earth to swallow him and his house. And he had no group that could help him apart from Allah, nor could he defend himself."
  28,82,"The next morning, those who had longed to be in his place the day before began to say: ‘Alas! It seems Allah provides abundantly to whom He wills among His servants and tightens it. Had Allah not been gracious to us, He would have also caused us to be swallowed. Alas! It seems the disbelievers will not prosper.’"
  28,83,That is the Abode of the Hereafter. We grant it to those who desire neither dominance upon the earth nor corruption. And the good end belongs to those who are God-conscious.
  28,84,"Whosoever brings a good deed, he shall receive (a reward) better than it. But whoever produces evil deed—those who commit misdeeds shall not be rewarded except for what they used to perform."
